      "value": "@{5baf6139b49f620eba95cdfa|full_name}: it can be fairly good, but the main issue is the buffer and translation between vrchat's systems, and windows media foundation. \nthere's another issue with unity itself running at around 44.1khz during runtime, so you should take advantage of that knowledge and tweak the bitrate.\nthe main difference here is that you do not need any intermediary server, it's direct from your pc if you open the outbound/inbound port.\nso, there's no server cost.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
