      "value": "@{5a60e3832478a072c83fa7ce|full_name}: Yes, streaming from your PC will be no server cost. Streaming 320kbps for 40 people will require 12.8Mbps bandwidth, it will be OK in most broadband connections.\nBut the problem is that the URL is fixed in your world, so you should have DNS domain record becase global IP will change in most connections for consumers (or upload your world everytime when your IP changed).\nOur most usage is open mic bar style music live. Difficult setup should be avoided but self hosting on your PC requires router configurations or UPnP. Maybe it will be achieved by developing dedicated streamer with functions of DDNS, UPnP, RTSP server and AAC encoder. But it's high development cost and we don't have stable RTSP server implementation when I tested at last year.\nRegarding sampling rate, it seems that Unity and AVProVideo handles it automatically. We streams 48kHz AAC from TopazChat Streamer and 44.1kHz AAC from OBS but everything is OK.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
